From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tobias Koch <tobias.koch@aeltra.eu>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 16:21:43 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] libfetch: fix leak in the fetchAppendURLList() error path

When strdup() failed, the cleanup loop counted down over i but freed
dst->urls[j].doc on every iteration -- always the entry whose strdup()
had just failed, and therefore always NULL.  The strings duplicated by
the preceding iterations were leaked.

Walk j back down to dst->length instead, which frees exactly the
entries that were successfully duplicated and stops before the one that
failed.

Signed-off-by: Tobias Koch <tobias.koch@aeltra.eu>
---
 libfetch/common.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libfetch/common.c b/libfetch/common.c
index b1ca550..ab09961 100644
--- a/libfetch/common.c
+++ b/libfetch/common.c
@@ -929,7 +929,7 @@ fetchAppendURLList(struct url_list *dst, const struct url_list *src)
 		dst->urls[j] = src->urls[i];
 		dst->urls[j].doc = strdup(src->urls[i].doc);
 		if (dst->urls[j].doc == NULL) {
-			while (i-- > 0)
+			while (j-- > dst->length)
 				free(dst->urls[j].doc);
 			fetch_syserr();
 			return -1;
